meta {
  name: 08-MissingStatusFilter
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

get {
  url: {{host}}/api/admin/verifications?type=OWNER_IDENTITY&status=APPROVED
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  type: OWNER_IDENTITY
  status: APPROVED
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{jwt}}
}

docs {
  # Probing: is `status` honoured even though the spec doesn't list it?

  My persona doc has me looking at recently-APPROVED items occasionally to
  spot-check approvals against new fraud patterns. The spec's `?type=`
  filter is the only documented one. I'm sending `status=APPROVED` to see
  if the server quietly supports it or just ignores it.

  Either outcome is a finding:
  - If it returns APPROVED items: the spec is lying about what filters
    exist (undocumented surface).
  - If it returns PENDING items (i.e. ignores my filter): I have no way
    to retrospectively review my own approvals — a major audit gap.
}
